261	---
262	
263	## Relationships
264	
265	```
266	boards (1) ──< board_members >── (N) users
267	boards (1) ──< lanes (N)
268	boards (1) ──< cards (N)      [denormalized]
269	lanes  (1) ──< cards (N)
270	cards  (1) ──< card_assignees >── (N) users
271	invitations (optional) ──> boards
272	invitations (optional) sets board_role on acceptance
273	```
274	
275	---
276	
277	## Position Invariants
278	
279	**Lane position**: unique per `board_id`; must always form the sequence 1…N after every
280	create, reorder, and delete.
281	
282	**Card position**: unique per `lane_id`; must always form the sequence 1…N after every
283	create, move, and delete.
284	
285	**Reorder algorithm** (example: move item from oldPos to newPos, oldPos > newPos):
286	
287	```sql
288	-- Step 1: shift up items in the gap
289	UPDATE lanes
290	SET position = position + 1
291	WHERE board_id = @boardId
292	  AND position >= @newPos
293	  AND position < @oldPos;
294	
295	-- Step 2: place the moved item
296	UPDATE lanes
297	SET position = @newPos, version = version + 1
298	WHERE id = @laneId
299	  AND version = @expectedVersion;  -- optimistic lock
300	```
301	
302	If step 2 returns 0 rows, the caller returns 409 Conflict.
303	
304	---
305	
306	## Value Objects (None New)
307	
308	`InvitationToken` from 001 is reused for board invitations — the same 256-bit random
309	token with SHA-256 hash. No new value objects are required for this feature.
